Result: BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 14s. The smoke confirmed the first signed EXPIRE_GENERATION was APPLIED with NOT_FOUND at Broker offset 2, the exact duplicate at offset 3 replayed the immutable NOT_FOUND result without resolving expiry authority again, the Target Store source frontier reached offset 3, and the Broker consumer-group committed offset reached 4. Both records returned APPLIED_AND_ACKED. The existing Target Worker Host lifecycle and initial Cancel source-turn checks also passed.

The single-node Broker briefly returned NOT_COORDINATOR during initial group-offset coordinator setup; the Kafka consumer rediscovered the coordinator, and the final committed-offset assertions passed.

Scope limits: expiry signing, time evidence, and authority resolution are test fixtures. This is a real single-node K1 Broker/Target Worker Source Apply check; it does not exercise the three-broker runner, Broker failover, expiry producer/Host assembly, production authority providers, ACK response loss, Owner takeover/recovery, or central C1 acceptance. The three-broker Docker runner was separately canceled before broker startup because the eclipse-temurin:21-jre base-image download remained near 2.1 MiB after about five minutes.
